  "decision": "FAIL / NO_CANDIDATE_ADMITTED / NO_ROBUST_STRATEGY_PASS. Both preregistered value-role substitutions showed positive return evidence relative to the frozen common-window V11 control but failed the frozen risk gates. IWD improved common-window CAGR from V11 8.195539% to 8.524869% and Sharpe from 0.874886 to 0.914479, beat V11 Sharpe in 5/7 fixed folds, and had paired-bootstrap P(CAGR>V11)=97.360% and P(Sharpe>V11)=99.180%. However, IWD MDD was 19.990634% and bootstrap MDD P97.5 was 26.524%, far above the frozen 10%/15% limits; cumulative 36-trial DSR probability was only 11.821%. VBR improved CAGR to 8.631507% and Sharpe to 0.906520 and also won 5/7 folds, with P(CAGR>V11)=95.205%, but P(Sharpe>V11)=88.505%, MDD was 21.618129%, bootstrap MDD P97.5 was 27.635%, and DSR was 11.084%. The trial additionally documents that restarting frozen V11 from cash at the 2004-01-30 common window materially changes its path and produces 21.291405% MDD, so this campaign is not evidence that a production V11 role substitution would retain the production V11 7.689054% MDD. Because the common-window restart design and asset substitutions were preregistered before performance, they may not be changed after seeing results. No S&P/IWD/VBR blend, substitution fraction, alternate common start, winner selection, or value timing rescue is permitted. The stable incremental return evidence from IWD is informative for future independent asset-role hypotheses, but neither current candidate is a validated strategy.",
